Discovery 1: Are process instances tagged with the APMID?
fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
| fieldsAdd tags
| filter contains(toString(tags), "APMID:APP0000XXXX")
| fields id, entity.name, tags
| limit 50


If this returns no records, run the same query on dt.entity.process_group. Tags are sometimes on the process group rather than the instance.

Discovery 2: Do the process CPU and memory metrics return data?
timeseries cpu = avg(dt.process.cpu.usage),
           mem = avg(dt.process.memory.working_set_size),
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}
| limit 10

Discovery 3: Are services tagged with the APMID?
fetch dt.entity.service
| fieldsAdd tags
| filter contains(toString(tags), "APMID:APP0000XXXX")
| fields id, entity.name, tags
| limit 50

Discovery 4: Does the response time metric return data?
timeseries rt = avg(dt.service.request.response_time),
           by:{dt.entity.service}
| limit 10




Visual: Table. Under No data, set the message to "All Claims endpoints available".

fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-30d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter event.status == "ACTIVE" and dt.davis.is_duplicate == false
| filter contains(lower(event.name), "monitor") and contains(lower(event.name), "outage")
| expand tag = entity_tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| expand eid = affected_entity_ids
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.http_check | fields id, httpName = entity.name ],
         sourceField: eid, lookupField: id, prefix: "h."
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.synthetic_test | fields id, browserName = entity.name ],
         sourceField: eid, lookupField: id, prefix: "b."
| fieldsAdd monitor = coalesce(h.httpName, b.browserName, eid),
            scope = if(contains(lower(event.name), "global"), "🔴 Global",
                    else: if(contains(lower(event.name), "local"), "🟠 Local", else: "🔴 Outage"))
| fieldsAdd appMonitor = concat(apmid, " | ", monitor),
            downFor = now() - event.start
| fields scope, appMonitor, event.name, display_id, downFor
| sort scope asc, downFor desc
